### B.2 PINN-ROM Training Procedure

```
Algorithm 2: Offline PINN-ROM Training with Adaptive Loss Weighting
Input:  High-fidelity simulation snapshots Q = {q(x,t_i)}_{i=1}^M
        Sensor calibration telemetry Y_cal
Output: Trained PINN-ROM weights Θ_ROM

PHASE 1 — POD BASIS CONSTRUCTION:
  C ← (1/M) Q Q^T
  Φ, Λ ← eigendecompose(C)
  r ← min{r: Σ_{i=1}^r λ_i / Σ λ_i ≥ 0.9999}
  Φ_r ← first r columns of Φ                    // retained POD basis

PHASE 2 — PINN TRAINING:
  Initialize network weights Θ by Xavier initialization
  Initialize adaptive weights w = {w_data, w_phys, w_BC, w_IC} = {1,1,1,1}
  Initialize Adam optimizer with lr = 10^{-3}, β_1=0.9, β_2=0.999

  for epoch = 1 to N_epochs:
    Sample N_d data points from Q
    Sample N_c collocation points from Ω × [0,T]
    Sample N_b boundary points from ∂Ω × [0,T]
    Sample N_i initial points from Ω × {0}

    L_data ← compute_data_loss(Θ, data_points, Q)
    L_phys ← compute_physics_residual(Θ, collocation_points)
    L_BC   ← compute_BC_loss(Θ, boundary_points)
    L_IC   ← compute_IC_loss(Θ, initial_points)

    // Adaptive weight update (NTK-informed)
    g_data ← ||∇_Θ L_data||,   g_phys ← ||∇_Θ L_phys||
    g_BC   ← ||∇_Θ L_BC||,     g_IC   ← ||∇_Θ L_IC||
    g_mean ← mean(g_data, g_phys, g_BC, g_IC)
    w_data ← g_mean/g_data;  w_phys ← g_mean/g_phys
    w_BC   ← g_mean/g_BC;    w_IC   ← g_mean/g_IC

    L_total ← w_data·L_data + w_phys·L_phys + w_BC·L_BC + w_IC·L_IC
    Θ ← Adam_update(Θ, ∇_Θ L_total)

    if epoch mod 1000 == 0:
      RMSE_val ← validate_on_holdout(Θ, Y_cal)
      if RMSE_val < 0.05: break               // 5% RMSE convergence criterion

  return Θ_ROM ← Θ
```

