### B.3 EVT Parameter Fitting and Online Adaptation

```
Algorithm 3: GPD Fitting and Online Threshold Adaptation
Input:  Training reconstruction errors R_train = {r_t}_{t=1}^{N_train}
        Sliding window buffer R_window (size N_adapt = 10,000)
Output: Alert thresholds τ_D, τ_PI, τ_C; updated GPD parameters (ξ, σ)

INITIALIZATION — OFFLINE FITTING:
  u ← percentile(R_train, 95)                   // POT threshold
  E_train ← {r - u: r ∈ R_train, r > u}         // exceedances
  ξ, σ ← MLE_GPD(E_train)                        // Maximum Likelihood Estimation
  τ_D  ← u + (σ/ξ)[(0.05)^{-ξ} − 1]            // 95th percentile of full distribution
  τ_PI ← u + (σ/ξ)[(0.001)^{-ξ} − 1]           // 99.9th percentile
  τ_C  ← u + (σ/ξ)[(0.0001)^{-ξ} − 1]          // 99.99th percentile

ONLINE ADAPTATION (executed every T_adapt = 10 s):
  R_window ← sliding_window_buffer.get_latest(N_adapt)
  R_nominal ← {r ∈ R_window: r < τ_D}           // exclude current anomalies
  if |R_nominal| > 0.8 · N_adapt:               // sufficient nominal data
    u_new ← percentile(R_nominal, 95)
    E_new ← {r - u_new: r ∈ R_nominal, r > u_new}
    ξ_new, σ_new ← MLE_GPD(E_new)
    // Exponential smoothing for stability
    ξ ← 0.9·ξ + 0.1·ξ_new
    σ ← 0.9·σ + 0.1·σ_new
    u ← 0.9·u + 0.1·u_new
    // Recompute thresholds
    update(τ_D, τ_PI, τ_C) using updated (ξ, σ, u)
    log_threshold_update(t, ξ, σ, u, τ_D, τ_PI, τ_C)
```

